{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "CLowl shared conformance fixture suite. Cases in the intersection where the two hand-maintained CLASS validators (TS CLowlMessage.validate / Python CLowlMessage.validate) agree. Consumed by both SDK runners plus fixtures/divergence_gate.py. Verdict vocab: valid | invalid | roundtrip_ok | roundtrip_mismatch.",
    "conformance_pair": "TS src/message.ts CLowlMessage.validate <-> Python clowl.py CLowlMessage.validate. NOT TS schema.ts validateSchema() (TS-only, stricter, no Python analog).",
    "kept_out": "Latent divergences reserved for OSA-1153 item 1: pid:null handling, unknown/extra fields, wrong clowl version (Python hardcodes 0.2), non-string tid/pid/det, float ts (TS accepts, Python rejects). Also 'missing mid' is NOT testable as invalid: both constructors auto-generate mid when falsy/nullish, so it validates valid in both. i02 tests the empty-string 'from' validate path instead (distinct from i04 missing-from construction path).",
    "classes": {
      "valid": "run validate() -> expect valid",
      "invalid": "run validate() (wrap construction in try/except -> invalid) -> expect invalid",
      "coercible": "invalid under strict validation today; expected_coercion annotates the intended OSA-1153 item 1 normalization -> expect invalid now",
      "roundtrip": "if invalid -> invalid; else compare parse->toDict() against expected_roundtrip -> roundtrip_ok | roundtrip_mismatch"
    }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
